  "title": "Realtime Face Video Enhancement: RTFVE and FSFVE for Compressed Video",
  "summary": "RTFVE introduces a model for real-time face video enhancement that integrates with video decoders and runs on ordinary CPUs, while FSFVE trains a model using 10 frames of a videocall to improve compressed video quality. Both models address bandwidth and computational limitations in low-bitrate video conferencing.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RTFVE can be incorporated with any video decoder and runs in real-time on ordinary CPUs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "FSFVE trains a model using 10 frames of a videocall to enhance compressed video.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both models significantly improve perceptual quality of compressed face video.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
